From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RitzDaCat <49771174+RitzDaCat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:37:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] sched: add wake signals

Port of the experimental-patches kernel feature series.
Use free flag bit 13. Clear tokens after the actual running callback in scx_start_task_running, including proxy donors; require root opt-in.
No performance or boot result is implied by this source port.

Private wake tags use 0x200/0x400 (shift 9), preserving token cause bits 0/1.
Compile-time assertions reject overlap with upstream wake flags, including WF_TTWU_RQ when present.
